===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|biology|systematics}} The study of the [[evolutionary]] history and [[relationship]]s among or within groups of [[organism]]s, through [[computational]] methods that focus on observed [[heritable]] traits.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:William Morton Wheeler|year=c. 1899|title=George Baur’s Life and Writings|journal=The American Naturalist|volume=33|page=16|text=Thereupon he went to Leipzig, and during the winter of 1880–81 and the following summer semester studied comparative anatomy with Leuckart, geology with Credner, and '''phylogenetics''' with Carus.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Stephen Bryant; Gerard Bouffard|title=Bioinformatics|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=Us9pAAAAMAAJ&q=%22An+especially+concise+introduction+to+molecular+phylogenetics+is+provided+by+Hillis+et+al.+(1993).+The+danger+of+generating+incorrect+results+is+inherently+greater+in+computational+phylogenetics+than+in+many+other+fields+of+science.%22&dq=%22An+especially+concise+introduction+to+molecular+phylogenetics+is+provided+by+Hillis+et+al.+(1993).+The+danger+of+generating+incorrect+results+is+inherently+greater+in+computational+phylogenetics+than+in+many+other+fields+of+science.%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj5nsr8wJ79AhVhcWwGHfGmAocQ6AF6BAgHEAI|page=366|publisher=Wiley
|passage=An especially concise introduction to molecular '''phylogenetics''' is provided by Hillis et al. (1993).<br>The danger of generating incorrect results is inherently greater in computational '''phylogenetics''' than in many other fields of science.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Emmanuel Paradis|title=Analysis of '''Phylogenetics''' and Evolution with R|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=FsScWggkW_cC&pg=PR7&dq=%22phylogenetics%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj_6bbBsp79AhXBqZUCHauaAi4Q6AF6BAgQEAI#v=onepage&q=%22phylogenetics%22&f=false|page=vii|publisher=Springer
|passage=A difficult task was to review the development of the many new packages contributing to '''phylogenetics''' and evolutionary biology.}}

